    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="1077" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg977"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157SA29/1302½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde Park</hi>, N. Y.</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-09-05">September 5,
                        1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Cordell</hi>: Will you see Frank Walsh on St.
                    Lawrence Treaty? I think he should <hi rendition="#italic">participate</hi> in
                    any further plans for negotiations with Canada.</p>
                <p>He is as you know Chairman of the N. Y. State Authority—&amp; the State owns the
                    bed of the River!</p>
                <p>I want to put the Treaty through.</p>
                <p>As ever</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
